From: Alexandr Mironov <7062352+alexandr-mironov@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5_pas: keep the modem proxy votes after handover (EXPERIMENT)

The vendor PIL holds vdd_cx/vdd_mss TURBO and xo for 10 s after the modem
starts; mainline drops them at handover. On vayu the modem now registers
and loses QLINK ~3 s later, before the first TX. Keep the votes (forever,
for the experiment) and see.
---

--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
@@ -387,6 +387,18 @@
 {
 	struct qcom_pas *pas = container_of(q6v5, struct qcom_pas, q6v5);
 
+	/*
+	 * EXPERIMENT (vayu tracker #6): keep the proxy votes (xo, cx, mss)
+	 * after handover. The vendor PIL holds them for 10 s
+	 * (qcom,proxy-timeout-ms); mainline drops them at handover. The modem
+	 * on vayu registers and then loses QLINK ~3 s later, before the first
+	 * TX - see whether the rails/clocks the AP stops voting for matter.
+	 */
+	if (q6v5->load_state && !strcmp(q6v5->load_state, "modem")) {
+		dev_info(pas->dev, "EXPERIMENT: keeping proxy votes after handover\n");
+		return;
+	}
+
 	if (pas->px_supply)
 		regulator_disable(pas->px_supply);
 	if (pas->cx_supply)
